@startuml seq-refund-failed
title PayLink - Refund a Failed Payment (release the hold)

' DECISIONS
' - Trigger: Payments starts this flow automatically whenever a payment enters Failed,
'   from SentToBiller (biller refuses) or from Unknown (retry, callback or reconciliation).
'   A customer-requested refund of a Completed payment (FR-27) is a different flow.
' - This is the ONLY place where the hold is released (Failed -> Refunded, section 2.5).
' - Accounts writes the ledger entries and the audit record in one transaction (FR-25).
'   audit_log is owned by SharedKernel types, written by Accounts for money movements.
' - Actor for the audit record of an automatic refund: "system".

participant Payments
participant "Accounts (Wallet)" as Accounts
participant Notifications

[-> Payments : paymentFailed(paymentId)
Payments -> Payments : load payment
alt Payment is not in state Failed (e.g. Unknown, Completed)
    Payments -> Payments : refuse, no refund
else Payment is in state Failed
    Payments -> Accounts : releaseHold(holdId, paymentId, actor = system, reason = "failed payment")
    note right of Accounts : ONE transaction:\n- compensating ledger entries\n  (held decreases, available increases by held amount)\n- audit record (who, when, why)
    alt Hold already released (duplicate trigger)
        Accounts --> Payments : alreadyReleased (no new entries)
    else Hold active
        Accounts --> Payments : holdReleased
    end
    Payments -> Payments : transition Failed -> Refunded
    Payments ->> Notifications : PaymentRefunded event\n(SMS + push, with reason)
end
@enduml